    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d852">

                <pb facs="0774" n="767" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg767"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11471: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-06T13:00:00-05:00">December 6, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>617. Your 1089, December 5, 10 a.m., just received. If the Japanese are willing
                    to withdraw the memorandum would it not be practicable <pb facs="0775" n="768"
                        xml:id="pg768"/> for the Commissioner of Police to withdraw his report to
                    the Municipal Council.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
